  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in a plane electromagnetic wave is given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>.<br />If this wave falls normally on a perfectly reflecting surface having an area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. If the radiation pressure exerted by the E.M. wave on the surface during a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>&nbsp;exposure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "354",
  "solution": {
